{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Machinery.QuantumTorusAJ","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Machinery.QuantumTorusAJ","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Machinery.QuantumTorus","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.AJFigureEight","lean:module:QOU.Mass.QDifferenceConfluentObstruction"],"declarations":14,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.QuantumTorusAJ.act2_ggm_add_c1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.QuantumTorusAJ.act2_ggm_add_c1","kind":"theorem","line":223,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/QuantumTorusAJ.lean#L223-L240","doc":"**Co-residence (the point of this file), operationally.**  Because\n`ggmElement …` and `c1Element …` are elements of the **same** ring\n`QuantumTorus (ℤ → K)`, their sum is again a torus element, and its `act2`\naction is the concrete order-2 operator obtained by adding the two kernels\ncoefficient-by-coefficient: `((a0−1) + (a1−1)L + (a2+c)L²)`.  This is a\nnon-vacuous witness that the two kernels live in one q-difference ring — the\nalgebraic sum only typechecks because of co-residence, and the result is an\nexplicit operator.  The proved five-route module distinction (slopes `{½,½}`\n(C1) vs `{−1,+1}` (GGM),\n`docs/audits/2026-07-20-qlift-gauge-gap-synthesis.md`) is therefore a\nstatement comparing these two concrete elements of the common ring; the\ninequivalence itself is not formalised here (Newton-polygon theory, outside\nMathlib). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.QuantumTorusAJ.c1Coeff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.QuantumTorusAJ.c1Coeff","kind":"def","line":215,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/QuantumTorusAJ.lean#L215-L219","doc":"The canonical C1 coefficient `c m = [m+2]_q` (the q-integer of the shifted\ncolour), matching `qlift_normalized_kernel_exists`'s `[n+2]_q` factor.  For\n`m ≥ 0` this is `QOU.Mass.QDifferenceConfluentObstruction.qint q (m+2)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.QuantumTorusAJ.act2_c1Element","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.QuantumTorusAJ.act2_c1Element","kind":"theorem","line":207,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/QuantumTorusAJ.lean#L207-L213","doc":"The C1 kernel torus element acts as `[m+2]_q σ² − σ − 1`:\n`act2 (c1Element c) b m = c m · b(m+2) − b(m+1) − b(m)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.QuantumTorusAJ.c1Element","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.QuantumTorusAJ.c1Element","kind":"def","line":190,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/QuantumTorusAJ.lean#L190-L205","doc":"**The C1 binding q-lift kernel as a torus element.**  With coefficient\nfunction `c : ℤ → K` (canonically `c m = [m+2]_q`, `c1Coeff`),\n`c1Element c = c·L² − L − 1` in the **same** `QuantumTorus (ℤ → K)` (written\nwith negated constant coefficients so only `+` is needed).  For `c m =\n[m+2]_q` this is the operator form of the proved kernel\n`[m+2]_q · b_{m+2} = b_{m+1} + b_m`\n(`QOU.Mass.QDifferenceConfluentObstruction.qlift_normalized_kernel_exists`),\nwhose Newton-polygon slopes at ∞ are the pure-isoclinic `{½,½}` — disjoint\nfrom the GGM/AJ carrier's `{−1,+1}` (five independent routes; see\n`docs/audits/2026-07-20-qlift-gauge-gap-synthesis.md`).  That module\ninequivalence is **not** proved here (Ramis–Sauloy–Zhang Newton-polygon\ntheory, outside Mathlib); this element only makes C1 **co-resident** with\n`ggmElement` so the distinction becomes a statement about two concrete\nelements of one ring. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.QuantumTorusAJ.act2_ggmElement_matches_figureEight","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.QuantumTorusAJ.act2_ggmElement_matches_figureEight","kind":"theorem","line":166,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/QuantumTorusAJ.lean#L166-L186","doc":"**GGM lives in the torus (compatibility theorem).**  The torus element\ncarrying the figure-eight coefficient functions maps under `act2` to the\n**exact** action of the concrete `figureEightOperator`\n(`∑_{j≤2} coeff_j(q, q^N)·J(N+j)`).  So the sorry-free GGM/AJ annihilator of\n`QOU.BraidKnot.AJFigureEight` is genuinely an element of the abstract\nquantum torus, and `act2` realises it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.QuantumTorusAJ.act2_ggmElement","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.QuantumTorusAJ.act2_ggmElement","kind":"theorem","line":158,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/QuantumTorusAJ.lean#L158-L164","doc":"The GGM torus element acts as the order-2 difference operator\n`a0 N · J N + a1 N · J(N+1) + a2 N · J(N+2)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.QuantumTorusAJ.coeffAt_ggmElement","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.QuantumTorusAJ.coeffAt_ggmElement","kind":"theorem","line":147,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/QuantumTorusAJ.lean#L147-L156","doc":"The torus element carries **exactly** the three operator coefficients:\n`coeffAt (ggmElement a0 a1 a2) j = a_j` for `j = 0,1,2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.QuantumTorusAJ.ggmElement","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.QuantumTorusAJ.ggmElement","kind":"def","line":141,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/QuantumTorusAJ.lean#L141-L145","doc":"**The order-2 GGM/AJ operator as a torus element.**  `ggmElement a0 a1 a2 =\na0 + a1·L + a2·L²` in `QuantumTorus (ℤ → K)` — the abstract shape of the\nfigure-eight annihilator (`AJFigureEight.figureEightOperator`, order 2). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.QuantumTorusAJ.act2_add","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.QuantumTorusAJ.act2_add","kind":"theorem","line":133,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/QuantumTorusAJ.lean#L133-L137","doc":"`act2` is additive in the torus element (it is a coefficient-linear\nreadout). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.QuantumTorusAJ.act2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.QuantumTorusAJ.act2","kind":"def","line":124,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/QuantumTorusAJ.lean#L124-L131","doc":"**The order-≤2 function-model action.**  A torus element `f` acts on a colour\ntower `J : ℤ → K` as the q-difference operator whose `L^j`-coefficient is the\ndiagonal `coeffAt f j` (`j = 0,1,2`): `L` shifts, `coeffAt f j` scales.  For\nan element supported in degrees `{0,1,2}` (every operator in this file) this\nis its full action; the corresponding q-Weyl relation for the `L, M`\ngenerators is `QuantumTorus.funcModel_qWeyl`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.QuantumTorusAJ.coeffAt_add","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.QuantumTorusAJ.coeffAt_add","kind":"theorem","line":119,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/QuantumTorusAJ.lean#L119-L122","doc":"Coefficient reading is additive: `coeffAt (f + g) = coeffAt f + coeffAt g`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.QuantumTorusAJ.sigma_diag","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.QuantumTorusAJ.sigma_diag","kind":"theorem","line":109,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/QuantumTorusAJ.lean#L109-L115","doc":"`σ` on the diagonal coefficient ring is the unit forward shift — the\noperator-level face of `L`'s q-Weyl action (`QuantumTorus.funcModel_qWeyl`,\n`L·M = q·M·L`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.QuantumTorusAJ.trans_smul_apply","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.QuantumTorusAJ.trans_smul_apply","kind":"theorem","line":106,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/QuantumTorusAJ.lean#L106-L107","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.QuantumTorusAJ.instTransAction","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.QuantumTorusAJ.instTransAction","kind":"instance","line":84,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/QuantumTorusAJ.lean#L84-L104","doc":"**The σ-twist as translation.**  The M-coefficient ring `A = ℤ → K` (a\ncolour-indexed diagonal operator) carries the L-degree group `Multiplicative\nℤ` acting by the shift `(ofAdd k) • a = fun N => a (N + k)`.  This is the\npaper's `σ(M) = c·M` realised on `M = q^N`: `σ(q^{·})(N) = q^{N+1} = q·q^N`,\ni.e. `c = q`.  A genuine `MulSemiringAction` (ring-automorphism action), so\n`QuantumTorus (ℤ → K)` is the skew-Laurent ring on this coefficient ring. ","signatureChunk":0}]}